+- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/metering/metric_definition.go`, `internal/controlplane/metering/traefik.go`, `internal/controlplane/metering/traefik_usage.go`, metering tests, `internal/controlplane/store/quota.go`, quota resource schema tests, `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0071_http_5xx_count_metering_resource.{up,down}.sql`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
+- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; focused RED/GREEN tests for `TestHTTP5xxCountMetricDefinition`, `TestTraefikAdapterCollectsWindowedPrometheusMetrics`, `TestTraefikUsageEmitterWritesHTTP5xxCountUsageEventsIdempotently`, and `TestQuotaResourceDomainEnforcesClosedSet`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -run TestMigrations ./...`; `go test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...`; `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...`; `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`; `go test -run TestRedaction ./...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`.
+- Results: All executed checks passed. `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` were not installed in this environment, so they were not run.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: Postgres-backed tests use the shared harness and skip when `YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL` is unset; the normal suite still runs without a live Dokploy server. `latency_p95_ms` remains the next tracked Traefik metric story.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Soft observability metrics follow the same tracked-metric vertical as `http_rps_peak_1m`: metric definition, derived Traefik sample when needed, `metricResource` mapping, quota-resource migration, quota resource constant, and idempotent usage-event emission.
+  - When adding a quota resource constant, update both `quotaResources` and `TestQuotaResourceValid`'s explicit constant list; the test fails fast if the constant set and membership map drift.
+  - Derived Traefik metrics should aggregate from normalized samples before checksums are copied onto the final collection, so derived samples inherit the same raw-window checksum as their source query set.
+---

