 ## Codebase Patterns
 - Soft/non-billing tracked metrics that must be customer-visible still flow through durable `usage_events` and `usage_counters`: `MetricDefinition.BillingGrade=false` controls billing semantics, not persistence; add a `quota_resource` constant/domain value when the metric must appear in usage APIs or billing export snapshots.
+- Derived Traefik tracked metrics should be created from normalized source samples before the collection checksum is copied onto final samples; new quota-resource metrics must update the SQL domain migration, `store.QuotaResource` constant, `quotaResources` membership map, and `TestQuotaResourceValid`'s explicit constant list together.
 - Invoice-period close snapshots compose existing billing surfaces instead of duplicating them: freeze `usage_counters` plus summed `usage_counter_adjustments` into `invoice_snapshot_items`, link the provider-neutral `billing_exports` row for export status/readback, store plan version + entitlement revision + source checksums for reproducibility, and handle corrections by marking the old snapshot `reopened` with an audit event before creating the next `close_version`.
 - Usage reconciliation lives at the metering boundary: inspect append-only `usage_events` window metadata, replay counters through `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents`, rely on `usage_counter_adjustments` for closed-period late usage idempotency, and record low-confidence gaps/quarantines/resets as value-free operator drift findings until a dedicated usage-drift taxonomy exists.
 - Metered overage hooks run at the usage-counter aggregation boundary, not inside quota/resource mutation code: runtime entitlement resolution carries plan/subscription metadata, `UsageCounterRepository.AggregateUsageEvents` stamps `usage_counters` with `entitlement_key`, `overage_policy_mode`, `overage_decision`, included/overage quantities, and an audit event, and `BillingExportRepository.Prepare` snapshots those fields into `billing_export_items` so provider adapters can bill/review overages without changing quota code.
@@ -38826,3 +38827,14 @@
   - `golangci-lint` is installed and enforces exported constant comments via revive; add comments with new exported enum values.
   - Optional security/release tools may be available through `scripts/verify.sh --strict --release` even when direct `command -v` checks do not find them in the shell.
 ---
+## 2026-05-19 15:20 +03 - BE-0588
+- What was implemented: Added `http_5xx_count` as a non-billing Traefik observability metric. The Traefik adapter derives service-level 5xx response counts from `traefik_service_requests_total` status-code series, attributed samples emit idempotent `usage_events`, aggregation produces `usage_counters`, and the closed `quota_resource` domain accepts the new metric key.
+- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/metering/metric_definition.go`, `internal/controlplane/metering/traefik.go`, `internal/controlplane/metering/traefik_usage.go`, metering tests, `internal/controlplane/store/quota.go`, quota resource schema tests, `internal/controlplane/store/migrate/migrations/0071_http_5xx_count_metering_resource.{up,down}.sql`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
+- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; focused RED/GREEN tests for `TestHTTP5xxCountMetricDefinition`, `TestTraefikAdapterCollectsWindowedPrometheusMetrics`, `TestTraefikUsageEmitterWritesHTTP5xxCountUsageEventsIdempotently`, and `TestQuotaResourceDomainEnforcesClosedSet`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -race ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test -run TestMigrations ./...`; `go test -run TestPolicyMatrix ./...`; `go test -run TestQuotaConcurrency ./...`; `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`; `go test -run TestRedaction ./...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`.
+- Results: All executed checks passed. `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` were not installed in this environment, so they were not run.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: Postgres-backed tests use the shared harness and skip when `YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL` is unset; the normal suite still runs without a live Dokploy server. `latency_p95_ms` remains the next tracked Traefik metric story.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - Soft observability metrics follow the same tracked-metric vertical as `http_rps_peak_1m`: metric definition, derived Traefik sample when needed, `metricResource` mapping, quota-resource migration, quota resource constant, and idempotent usage-event emission.
+  - When adding a quota resource constant, update both `quotaResources` and `TestQuotaResourceValid`'s explicit constant list; the test fails fast if the constant set and membership map drift.
+  - Derived Traefik metrics should aggregate from normalized samples before checksums are copied onto the final collection, so derived samples inherit the same raw-window checksum as their source query set.
